                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Great game but the steam version sucks. Get the GOG version instead. It's more stable, it can run at 60+ fps without having to make obscure ini tweaks, the textures are higher resolution, it's more compatible with mods, and the DLC content actually works together by default. For some god forsaken reason, the steam version lists Spore (Base Game), Creepy & Cute Parts DLC, and Galactic Adventures as if they're each separate games instead of addon content for the base game. You can fix this by installing Galactic Adventures (you do NOT need to install the base game), then installing Creepy & Cute, and merging C&C's folders into your Galactic Adventures install folder. Or... just buy the GOG version because this one is dogshit.",
